# AWS NAT Instance Setup for Private EC2 Internet Access

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates how to provide internet access to an Amazon EC2 instance running in a private subnet using a **NAT Instance** instead of a NAT Gateway.

The solution was implemented in AWS using the `us-east-1` region. A public subnet was created to host an Amazon Linux 2023 NAT instance, which forwards traffic from the private subnet to the internet.

The configuration was verified by confirming that the private EC2 instance successfully uploaded `datacenter-test.txt` to the designated Amazon S3 bucket.

## Objectives

* Create a public subnet named `datacenter-pub-subnet`.

* Launch an Amazon Linux 2023 EC2 instance named `datacenter-nat-instance`.

* Configure a custom security group for the NAT instance.

* Enable IP forwarding and configure NAT masquerading using `iptables`.

* Disable source/destination checking on the NAT instance.

* Configure the public and private route tables.

* Verify internet access by checking the S3 test file.

